# Spotler MailPro Product Context Skill

## Purpose

Use this Skill when designing or redesigning product features for Spotler MailPro.

This Skill gives Figma Make product context for Spotler MailPro so it can make better UX and product decisions without starting from generic email marketing, automation, or SaaS assumptions. It explains what the product is, who uses it, how it works, which workflows matter, which terminology to use, and what product logic should be preserved.

This is not a Design System Skill. Do not use this Skill for visual styling, component rules, typography, spacing, colours, or layout patterns. Use the separate Spotler Design System Skill or attached design system documentation for those decisions.

---

## Product Summary

Spotler MailPro is an advanced email marketing platform for organisations with complex email programmes, large contact databases, multiple brands, multiple business units, approval needs, or advanced data structures.

It helps marketing teams manage email content, data, automation, permissions, approvals, reporting, and campaign operations centrally.

MailPro is designed for teams that need more structure, control, and scalability than basic email tools provide. It supports reusable content, central template and asset management, relational data, advanced personalisation, visual automation flows, role-based access, approval workflows, campaign reporting, exportable reports, and integrations with the broader Spotler ecosystem.

The product helps organisations move from fragmented email processes, duplicated templates, flat contact lists, and manual workflows to a structured, governed, data-driven email marketing operation.

---

## Core Problem Spotler MailPro Solves

Spotler MailPro solves the problems that appear when email marketing becomes complex and needs to scale.

Common problems include:

- Fragmented data
- Duplicate templates
- Recreated content across teams or brands
- Manual campaign processes
- Content updates that take too long
- Approvals happening outside the system
- Inconsistent messaging across brands or departments
- Compliance risks
- Flat contact lists that cannot represent complex relationships
- Difficult-to-share reports
- Insights spread across different systems
- Too much operational effort
- Reliance on external tools or technical workflows

Spotler MailPro addresses these challenges by centralising content, structuring data through relational databases, supporting reusable modules, enabling visual automation flows, and providing built-in governance through roles, permissions, and approval workflows.

The result is faster campaign creation, better control, clearer insight, more consistent communication, and more scalable email operations.

---

## Target Users and User Roles

Spotler MailPro is primarily used by marketing teams that manage complex email programmes.

### Primary users

#### Email marketer

An email marketer uses MailPro to create campaigns, manage content, personalise messages, automate journeys, and analyse results.

Goals:

- Build emails efficiently
- Reuse proven content and modules
- Personalise campaigns with data
- Automate recurring or triggered emails
- Analyse campaign performance
- Reduce manual work

Typical needs:

- Drag-and-drop email editor
- Templates
- Reusable modules
- Personalisation filters
- Visual automation flow builder
- Reports
- A/B testing

---

#### Marketing operations user

A marketing operations user manages structured campaign processes, data, permissions, reporting, and operational consistency.

Goals:

- Keep campaign operations scalable
- Reduce manual technical workflows
- Manage relational data structures
- Maintain content governance
- Support multiple brands or teams
- Keep reporting shareable and reliable

Typical needs:

- Relational databases
- Collections
- Data filters
- Account configuration
- Permission setup
- Approval workflow configuration
- Exportable reports

---

#### Central marketing team

A central marketing team supports multiple brands, departments, local teams, or business units.

Goals:

- Maintain central control
- Provide reusable templates and assets
- Safeguard brand consistency
- Support local execution
- Ensure approvals before sending
- Reduce duplicated work

Typical needs:

- Brand-specific templates
- Central asset libraries
- Reusable modules
- Role-based access
- Approval workflows
- Shared campaign reporting

---

#### Local or brand marketer

A local or brand marketer creates campaigns within the boundaries set by the central team.

Goals:

- Create brand-specific campaigns quickly
- Use approved templates and modules
- Adapt content for a specific audience or brand
- Follow approval processes
- Send compliant communications

Typical needs:

- Access to correct brand templates
- Reusable content modules
- Clear approval status
- Campaign editing
- Personalisation options
- Simple reporting

---

#### Campaign manager

A campaign manager manages one-off campaigns, recurring campaigns, automated journeys, and optimisation.

Goals:

- Plan and execute campaigns
- Set up automation flows
- Use data for targeting
- Test subject lines and content
- Share results with stakeholders

Typical needs:

- Campaign overview
- Visual flow builder
- Trigger-based sending
- A/B testing
- Campaign summaries
- Exportable reports

